                        Email: <span>stephan.emmermann[at]gmail.com</span>
                    </address>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">2. Core Principle: Local-First</h2>
            <p>
                LetterLoom is a desktop application.
                <strong>
                    Your CV, job ads, cover letters, settings and local
                    database are stored exclusively on your own device
                </strong> (under
                <code>%LocalAppData%\NetAi.LetterLoom</code>). We do not operate a server that receives or stores
                your application documents.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                There is no telemetry, no analytics, and no usage tracking built into the application.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">3. Data Processed on Your Device</h2>
            <p>The following data remains on your device and is not transmitted to us:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>CV content (Markdown text)</li>
                <li>Job advertisements (URLs and pasted text)</li>
                <li>Generated prompts, phase outputs, and cover letters</li>
                <li>Skills table and application settings</li>
                <li>API keys for third-party LLM endpoints (currently stored in <code>settings.json</code> on your device)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-0">
                You are responsible for the security of your device and for the confidentiality of any API keys you enter.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">4. LLM Processing: Local or Third-Party API</h2>
            <p>
                LetterLoom can use either a <strong>local LLM</strong> (running on your machine via
                <code>llama-server</code>) or an <strong>OpenAI-compatible API endpoint that you configure yourself</strong>.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Local mode:</strong> All prompt processing happens on your device. No data leaves your machine.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>API mode:</strong> When you configure an external API endpoint, the content you submit
                    (CV excerpts, job ad text, prompts) is transmitted to that endpoint. You choose the provider;
                    their privacy policy and data processing terms apply.
                    <strong>
                        We do not control and are not
                        responsible for the data processing practices of the API provider you select.
                    </strong>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Please review the privacy policy of your chosen LLM provider before submitting personal data.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">5. Payment Processing via Paddle</h2>
            <p>
                Purchases of LetterLoom are processed by <strong>Paddle.com Market Ltd</strong> (“Paddle”) as
                Merchant of Record. Paddle is the legal seller of the product for consumer-law purposes.
            </p>
            <p>
                When you make a purchase, Paddle collects and processes payment data (name, email, billing address,
                payment method, tax information) as an independent controller. We do not receive your full payment
                details. We may receive limited transaction metadata (e.g. license status, country, order reference)
                to provide support and manage licenses.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Paddle’s privacy practices are governed by Paddle’s own policies:
                <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" class="link-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">paddle.com/legal/privacy</a>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">6. Update Notifications (Future)</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                The current version contains no automatic update check. If a future version adds an update notification,
                it will be documented here before the feature is activated. Any such check would transmit only
                technical version information, not your application content.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">7. Legal Bases</h2>
            <dl class="row">
                <dt class="col-sm-4">Provision of the software</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-8">Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (contract performance)</dd>

                <dt class="col-sm-4">Payment and tax compliance (via Paddle)</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-8">Art. 6(1)(b) and (c) GDPR</dd>

                <dt class="col-sm-4">Support communication</dt>
                <dd class="col-sm-8">Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR (legitimate interest)</dd>
            </dl>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">8. Recipients</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                We do not share your application content with third parties. The only external recipient involved in
                a purchase is <strong>Paddle</strong> (payment processing). If you choose an external LLM API,
                data is transmitted to that provider at your direction.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">9. Retention</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Application data on your device remains until you delete it or uninstall the application.
                Payment-related records held by Paddle are retained by Paddle in accordance with statutory
                retention obligations.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">10. Your Rights</h2>
            <p>You have the rights under the GDPR, including:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
                <li>Rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
                <li>Erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
                <li>Restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
                <li>Data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
                <li>Objection (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
                <li>Withdrawal of consent (Art. 7(3) GDPR)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                To exercise these rights, contact
                <span>stephan.emmermann[at]gmail.com</span>.
                For payment-data requests, please contact Paddle directly.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
                The competent authority for the provider is:
            </p>
            <address class="mt-2 mb-0">
                Die Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und für das Recht auf Akteneinsicht Brandenburg<br/>
                Stahnsdorfer Damm 77<br/>
                14532 Kleinmachnow<br/>
                Germany<br/>
                <a href="mailto:Poststelle@LDA.Brandenburg.de" class="link-primary">Poststelle@LDA.Brandenburg.de</a>
            </address>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">11. Accessibility (BFSG)</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                The German Accessibility Strengthening Act (BFSG) applies to consumer-facing software.
                We are working to align the application with the applicable accessibility requirements.
                If you encounter an accessibility barrier, please contact us at the email address above.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h4 mb-3">12. Changes</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in the application or legal requirements.
                The current version is always available at this page.
            </p>
        </section>

